@startuml Deal Management Application - Container Diagram

' Define the styles
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #e3f2fd
skinparam componentBorderColor #1976d2
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #f3e5f5
skinparam databaseBorderColor #7b1fa2
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #fff3e0
skinparam actorBorderColor #f57c00
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d

' Title
title Deal Management Application - Container Diagram (C4 Level 2)

' Actor
actor "User\n(Sales Rep/Manager)" as user <<Person>> #fff3e0

' System boundary
package "Deal Management Application" {

    ' Web Application Container
    component "Embedded Tomcat\nWeb Server" as tomcat <<Container: Apache Tomcat 10.1>> #e3f2fd

    ' REST API Container
    component "REST API" as api <<Container: Jakarta Servlets>> #e3f2fd

    ' Business Logic Container
    component "Business Logic\nLayer" as service <<Container: Java Classes>> #e3f2fd

    ' Data Access Container
    component "Data Access\nLayer" as repository <<Container: JDBC Repositories>> #e3f2fd

    ' H2 Console Container
    component "H2 Database\nConsole" as h2console <<Container: Web Interface>> #fff9c4
}

' Database
database "H2 Embedded\nDatabase" as db <<Database: H2>> #f3e5f5

' Relationships - User interactions
user --> tomcat : Makes HTTP requests\n[HTTPS/HTTP]
tomcat --> api : Routes to servlet
api --> service : Calls business methods
service --> repository : Persists/retrieves data
repository --> db : Executes SQL\n[JDBC]

' H2 Console interactions
user ..> h2console : Accesses for debugging\n[HTTP]
h2console ..> db : Queries database\n[JDBC]

' Component notes
note right of tomcat
  <b>Web Server</b>

  Embedded servlet container:
  • Hosts REST API
  • Manages HTTP lifecycle
  • Routes requests to servlets
  • Serves H2 console

  <b>Technology:</b>
  Apache Tomcat 10.1 (embedded)
end note

note right of api
  <b>REST API Layer</b>

  Provides HTTP endpoints for:
  • Deal CRUD operations
  • Query and filtering
  • Business operations (close deal)

  <b>Technology:</b>
  • Jakarta Servlets
  • Gson for JSON
  • HTTP methods: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE

  <b>Endpoints:</b>
  /api/v1/integration/deals
end note

note left of service
  <b>Service Layer</b>

  Encapsulates business rules:
  • Deal validation
  • Status transitions
  • Business constraints
  • Complex queries

  <b>Key Classes:</b>
  • DealService
  • UserService

  <b>Responsibilities:</b>
  • Enforce "deal value must be positive"
  • Validate "can only delete OPEN deals"
  • Calculate pipeline metrics
end note

note left of repository
  <b>Repository Layer</b>

  Manages data persistence:
  • SQL query execution
  • Object-relational mapping
  • Transaction management

  <b>Key Classes:</b>
  • H2DealRepository
  • H2UserRepository
  • DatabaseManager

  <b>Pattern:</b>
  Repository Pattern with
  Repository<T> interface
end note

note right of h2console
  <b>Development Tool</b>

  Web-based SQL interface:
  • Query execution
  • Schema inspection
  • Data browsing

  <b>URL:</b>
  /h2-console
end note

note bottom of db
  <b>Persistence Store</b>

  File-based relational database:
  • deals table (deal records)
  • users table (user accounts)
  • Embedded in application

  <b>Technology:</b>
  H2 Database Engine

  <b>Connection:</b>
  jdbc:h2:./data/commissions

  <b>Schema:</b>
  Auto-initialized on startup
end note

note as N1
  <b>HTTP Request Flow</b>

  User → Tomcat → API → Service → Repository → Database

  Example: POST /api/v1/integration/deals
  1. User sends JSON payload
  2. Tomcat receives HTTP request
  3. API parses request, validates format
  4. Service validates business rules
  5. Repository executes SQL INSERT
  6. Database persists data
  7. Response flows back: DB → Repo → Service → API → Tomcat → User
end note

legend right
  <b>C4 Model - Level 2: Container Diagram</b>

  Zooms into the Deal Management Application to show
  the high-level technical building blocks (containers).

  <b>Container Definition:</b>
  A container is a separately runnable/deployable unit
  that executes code or stores data.

  <b>This Diagram Shows:</b>
  • Web Server (Tomcat) - executes servlets
  • REST API - handles HTTP requests
  • Business Logic - enforces rules
  • Data Access - manages persistence
  • H2 Console - development tool
  • Database - stores data

  <b>Key Architectural Patterns:</b>
  • Layered Architecture (API → Service → Repository)
  • Embedded Server (Tomcat runs in-process)
  • Repository Pattern (data access abstraction)
  • Dependency Injection (manual)

  <b>Audience:</b>
  • Software architects
  • Developers
  • Technical leads

  <b>Technology Stack:</b>
  • Java 21
  • Jakarta Servlets
  • JDBC
  • H2 Database
  • Gson
  • SLF4J/Logback
endlegend

@enduml